criptors, extension keys, identities and immutable generations as the section defines them), Section 7.8 (the session-adapter operations that produce them: capture-plan, capture, normalize with fresh isolated sinks; probe/manifest/discover/inspect read-only), and Section 10.2 content-addressed blobs (Blob Descriptor identity, byte-count agreement, no-replace install through the landed durable-write discipline). Exclusion handoff (row 21 of TASK-260909-2ez769, read TASK-260909-2ez769_exclusion-handoff.md on that task): the bundle/manifest member allowlist MUST reject hosttrust.MatchExcludedFromReplication and ExcludedConfigDirName matches at construction, with a constructor negative test per excluded class. Deliver: closed-shape validators registered through canonicaljson (replace the rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape registrations only if the shape owner's tests and census admit it — otherwise validate in your package and say so), construction/normalization entry points that produce byte-identical outputs for identical inputs, refusals for every closed-shape rule (unknown class, included item with a reason, excluded item with content, unknown class making raw_complete false, credential/auth/runtime/lock classes never included, unsorted or duplicate entries, unsanitized native key, fabricated AX identity, excluded-path members), and the capture boundary rules. Scope is 13 points: slice by contract if needed (Raw Object Manifest + Capture Items + exclusion first; Canonical Session/Event and generations second) and enumerate what remains for the siblings.\n2|COMMON CONTRACT (first leaf of a Story on trunk 7efe385 or later). Normative authority: the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md headings named below; the v0.7.0 adoption (STORY-260916-3uqbwq) is landing during your run and is byte-identical in these sections — if it has landed when you refresh, cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers. Reuse the landed owners (canonicaljson closed shapes, scalar, sessrepo/sessstate/sessquery, sessckpt, matjournal, crashgate, fencing, sessprofile, provhost/resumesmoke, hosttrust/peeridentity/sshtransport, rpcwire/hostchannel, sessadapter, terminalbackend, localstore, secprim/secconftest) — never fork a second model; extend or adopt. Traceability: do NOT edit internal/traceability (ownership registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) in this first leaf — the Story's FINAL leaf carries the registry bindings and re-pin once the v0.7.0 registry is on trunk; document your clause coverage in a package-local TRACEABILITY.md and the conformance matrix instead. Evidence contract (repository DoD): every AC row driven through a production entry by a named committed test with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites; negatives for every refusal; a narrowing mutant per gate executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__); crash/idempotency evidence for every durable write (landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern) or an explicit purity bound; conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to a test or a stated bound; README package section with test commands and NO capability/CLI claim (no ax command exists); LOGBOOK entry newest-first. Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q forked from current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED; never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-24z2b3` (LOGBOOK append conflicts are resolved with --replay-resolutions: copy the retained resolution-template.json header and add {\"checkpoint_oid\": <REBASE_HEAD original checkpoint>, \"path\": \"LOGBOOK.md\", \"sha256\": <hex of the full replacement>, \"content\": <base64>} keeping every entry newest-first), then audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old-base> <new-base>` that appears in your git status and restore trunk content by hand (README/LOGBOOK purely additive; task-board.config.json == HEAD); before handoff `git status` shows only candidate paths. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured 26-command validation suite once before handoff (command 21 is `cataloggen -adopted … -check`); hand off no later than 3.5 hours in — if the full scope cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining items enumerated precisely in the results. Attach TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md, TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-24z2b3 --role developer` and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be claude-opus-5 max.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
