{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6f3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0d3-448d-7fa1-9a80-daada0956017"},"sequence":468,"recorded_at":1780531400000931,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0d44a5675ed8bd52eaa0268f2d4","text":"Read text file `/tmp/rev2/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-24z2b3 Results — implement-clone-bundle-and-canonical-session-types\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story\n4|worktree (`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q`); no commit on the\n5|Story branch. This is attempt 2 (run RUN-260917-959ae5): rev1 CR\n6|validation failed at command 5/27 (`go test ./... -race -count=1`,\n7|`internal/sessquery` 600s default-timeout). The candidate below is\n8|unchanged from rev1 except one LOGBOOK wording fix; the failure is\n9|proven pre-existing and environmental (see \"rev1 failure\" section).\n10|\n11|## Delivered\n12|\n13|`internal/clonebundle` (new package, 11 production files) implements\n14|the Section 13.14.1 clone capture contracts over the landed owners:\n15|\n16|- Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0 (`rawmanifest.go`): closed\n17|  envelope, omit-self ID, sorted unique entries, total_bytes sum,\n18|  raw class subset, descriptor agreement at construction.\n19|- Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (`capturebuild.go`, `captureitem.go`,\n20|  `boundary.go`): Source Basis union, Capture Boundary union with\n21|  stable-proof coupling, sorted Capture Items, exact excluded\n22|  classes, core-derived `raw_complete`, maximal_safe and G2 gates.\n23|- Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors (`session.go`): one main actor,\n24|  ordered unique event IDs, head subset.\n25|- Canonical Event 1.0.0 (`event.go`): 26-kind vocabulary,\n26|  visibility, kind-selected payload with content-block rules,\n27|  SourceEvidence with synthesized coupling, sorted unique raw refs,\n28|  ordinal contiguity.\n29|- Identities (`identity.go`): NativeIdentity, WorkspaceBinding,\n30|  shared native-key sanitizer (no absolute path, UUIDv7/AX\n31|  confusion, embedded credentials, AX markers, control chars).\n32|- Immutable generations (`generation.go`): opaque tokens with exact\n33|  equality, digest-equality comparison.\n34|- Raw evidence descriptors (`blobref.go`): Blob Descriptor shape +\n35|  identity via `canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity` with a local\n36|  claim comparison (never the attesting entry, per the provhost\n37|  no-attestation bound), blob/size agreement, install through\n38|  `localstore.PutBlob`.\n39|\n40|Also: `TRACEABILITY.md` (clause map), `testdata/mutant_harness.py`\n41|(17 narrowing + 1 control), README package section (test commands,\n42|no capability claim), LOGBOOK entry (newest-first).\n43|\n44|## AC coverage: 18 of 18 rows driven\n45|\n46|See `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md`: every row names its\n47|production call site and driving test. No prose-only claims.\n48|\n49|## Validation reran in attempt 2 (this run, final tree)\n50|\n51|- `gofmt` check / `go build ./...` / `go vet ./...`: PASS\n52|  (log `static-gates.log`)\n53|- `go test ./internal/clonebundle/ -count=1`: PASS\n54|  (log `pkg-test.log`)\n55|- `go test ./internal/clonebundle/ -race -count=1`: PASS\n56|  (log `pkg-race.log`)\n57|- `go test ./internal/clonebundle/ -cover -count=1`: PASS, 82.2%\n58|  statements (log `pkg-cover.log`)\n59|- Mutant harness: 17 KILLED + 1 SURVIVED control, exit 0,\n60|  `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__` (log `mutants.log`)\n61|- Fuzz smoke 14/14 targets: PASS (log `static-gates.log`)\n62|- `tracecheck`: PASS; `cataloggen -adopted -check`: PASS\n63|  (log `static-gates.log`)\n64|- `GOOS=linux` / `GOOS=windows` builds: PASS (log `static-gates.log`)\n65|- JSON validation, `task-board validate` (exit 0),\n66|  `git diff --check`: PASS (log `static-gates.log`)\n67|- `go test ./internal/sessquery -count=1` (no race): PASS\n68|  (log `sessquery-norace.log`)\n69|\n70|Accepted from rev1 attached evidence (not rerun: full-suite runs\n71|exceed the single-call bound and the tree is unchanged since rev1\n72|except the LOGBOOK wording fix): `go test ./... -count=1` PASS\n73|38/38, `go test ./... -cover` PASS, rev1 race log showing\n74|`internal/clonebundle ok` plus the `sessquery` timeout. The CR\n75|validation reruns the full suite automatically.\n76|\n77|## rev1 failure: `sessquery` -race 600s timeout is pre-existing\n78|\n79|`internal/sessquery` needs ~630s under `-race` on this host (rev1\n80|measured 630s with `-timeout 25m`, no DATA RACE, no failing\n81|assertion) against the 600s default `go test` timeout. Attempt-2\n82|proof that the candidate does not cause it:\n83|\n84|- Same-shard race comparison, back to back:\n85|  `go test ./internal/sessquery -race -count=1 -run\n86|  TestReview11ReferencedTemporalAuthority` → worktree (candidate\n87|  present) 65.6s PASS, clean trunk archive at the same commit\n88|  (no candidate) 66.8s PASS (logs `shard-worktree.log`,\n89|  `shard-trunk.log`). Identical within host noise.\n90|- No package outside `internal/clonebundle` imports it\n91|  (`NO_EXTERNAL_IMPORTERS`, see `static-gates.log`), so no other\n92|  package's test binary changes.\n93|- Full `sessquery` without race PASSES (log\n94|  `sessquery-norace.log`); host load averaged 19–40 during these\n95|  runs (log `host-load.txt`, shared machine).\n96|- `sessquery` is outside this task's story boundary; no\n97|  `sessquery` file was touched. The default-timeout race gate\n98|  stays red on `sessquery` on this machine by host slowness,\n99|  reported as a finding, not fixed by weakening another story's\n100|  tests.\n101|\n102|## Notable finding (rev1, retained)\n103|\n104|The first full-suite run reddened\n105|`provhost.TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`: that\n106|census forbids any non-test call to\n107|`canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity` outside `internal/sessrepo`.\n108|Fixed at the root cause following the landed `sessprofile` precedent:\n109|`blobref.go` now uses `CalculateObjectIdentity` (shape + digest)\n110|with a local claim comparison and never calls the attesting entry.\n111|A wrong-claim negative plus narrowing mutant `N-descriptor-claim`\n112|pin the new gate. No test was weakened; `provhost` and the full\n113|suite are green. (Attempt 2 additionally corrected the LOGBOOK\n114|entry's stale `VerifyObjectIdentity` mention to match the shipped\n115|gate; the only tree change since rev1.)\n116|\n117|## Bounds for siblings (not waived)\n118|\n119|- Per-kind event payload fact registries past the envelope\n120|  (`checkPayload`); maximal_safe planning past the refusal gate;\n121|  G2 admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`; Section 7.8\n122|  operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`); `internal/traceability`\n123|  bindings + re-pin (FINAL leaf).\n124|\n125|## Base refresh\n126|\n127|Before handoff, `origin/main` advanced 7efe385 → 888ae3d\n128|(`TASK-260917-3f8mkd: give the race gate an explicit 25m timeout`,\n129|config-only). Ran `task-board worktree refresh-candidate`, restored\n130|`task-board.config.json` to HEAD per the candidate audit rule, and\n131|re-verified `go build ./...` + the package suite on the new base\n132|(PASS). The refresh resolves the rev1 failure mode at the suite\n133|level; all attempt-2 logs above were captured on 7efe385 and are\n134|unaffected (no production file differs between the bases).\n135|\n136|## Attachments\n137|\n138|- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md` (unchanged from rev1)\n139|- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (attempt-2 logs:\n140|  package suite, mutants, static gates, sessquery shard pair,\n141|  sessquery non-race, host load, file manifest)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6f5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0d3-448d-7fa1-9a80-daada0956017"},"sequence":469,"recorded_at":1780531400000933,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0d44bf077ea9199646f422209e9","text":"Read text file `/tmp/rev2/matrix.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-24z2b3 Conformance Matrix\n2|\n3|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1.\n4|Package: `internal/clonebundle`. Normative spec text is quoted from the\n5|pinned file; the prose here maps, never restates.\n6|\n7|## AC coverage: 18 of 18 rows driven\n8|\n9|Every row is driven through the named production entry point by the\n10|named committed test. Prose ratio: **18 of 18 AC rows driven**.\n11|\n12|| # | AC row | Production call site | Named test |\n13||---|---|---|---|\n14|| 1 | Raw Object Manifest closed envelope + omit-self ID | `BuildRawObjectManifest`, `DecodeRawObjectManifest` | `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `TestRawManifestRefusals/decode` |\n15|| 2 | RawObjectEntry class subset (credential/auth/runtime/lock forbidden) | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries`, `validRawEntryClass` | `TestRawManifestRefusals/build` (unknown + 4 forbidden-class rows) |\n16|| 3 | Sorted unique entries, total_bytes = sum | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries` | `TestRawManifestRefusals` (unsorted, duplicate, total mismatch) |\n17|| 4 | Sanitized native keys, never an AX Session ID | `SanitizeNativeKey` | `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer` + key rows in raw/capture/session/event tables |\n18|| 5 | Row-21 exclusion allowlist at construction | `refuseExcludedMember` | `TestRawManifestExcludesTrustMaterial`, `TestCaptureManifestExcludesTrustMaterial` |\n19|| 6 | Capture Manifest envelope + omit-self ID | `BuildCaptureManifest`, `DecodeCaptureManifest` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestDerivesRawComplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/decode` |\n20|| 7 | CaptureItem 9-class vocabulary + included/excluded content rule | `ValidCaptureClass`, `checkItemDisposition` | `TestCaptureClassVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestCaptureItemRefusals` |\n21|| 8 | Always-excluded classes never included | `alwaysExcludedClass` | `TestCaptureItemRefusals` (credential, machine_auth, runtime_state, transient_lock rows) |\n22|| 9 | excluded_classes exactly the excluded-row classes | `excludedRowClasses`, `excludedClassesExact` | `TestExcludedClassesExactGate`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/decode` (extra, missing, unsorted, unknown) |\n23|| 10 | Core-derived raw_complete + plan/object reconciliation | `deriveRawComplete`, `VerifyCaptureReconciliation` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestDerivesRawComplete`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\n24|| 11 | Unknown blocks maximal_safe | `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\n25|| 12 | Capture Source Basis closed union | `DecodeSourceBasis`, `buildSourceBasis` | `TestSourceBasisRefusals` |\n26|| 13 | Capture Boundary union + stable-proof coupling | `DecodeCaptureBoundary`, `buildBoundary`, `checkProofCoupling` | `TestBoundaryRefusals`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n27|| 14 | Unstable is core-created; G2 rejects it | `buildBoundary` (Core), `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestBoundaryRefusals/build_core-only_unstable`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n28|| 15 | NativeIdentity + WorkspaceBinding identities | `DecodeNativeIdentity`, `EncodeNativeIdentity`, `IdentityDigest`, `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` | `TestNativeIdentityRoundTrip`, `TestIdentityDigestIsStable`, `TestIdentityRefusals` |\n29|| 16 | Canonical Session + Actor rules (one main, event/head IDs) | `BuildCanonicalSession`, `DecodeCanonicalSession` | `TestBuildCanonicalSessionRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalSessionRefusals` |\n30|| 17 | Canonical Event + SourceEvidence + raw refs + ordinals + generations | `BuildCanonicalEvent`, `DecodeCanonicalEvent`, `DecodeSourceEvidence`, `checkPayload`, `CheckOrdinalContiguity`, `ParseGeneration` | `TestEventKindVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals`, `TestOrdinalContiguity`, `TestGenerationRefusals` |\n31|| 18 | Blob Descriptor identity + byte-count agreement + no-replace install | `VerifyDescriptorAgreement`, `InstallRawBlob`, `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` | `TestBlobAgreementRefusals`, `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip` |\n32|\n33|## Negative/refusal evidence\n34|\n35|Every refusal above fails when the gate admits what it must reject:\n36|the 17 narrowing mutants in `internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py`\n37|weaken each gate to admit exactly one forbidden member and the named\n38|killer fails (17 KILLED, 1 harmless SURVIVED control). Per-plant\n39|results are in the producer evidence tar.\n40|\n41|## Landed-owner reuse (not new behavior, cited not counted)\n42|\n43|| Scope | Owner | Evidence |\n44||---|---|---|\n45|| Section 7.8 operation frames (capture-plan/capture/normalize fresh isolated sinks; probe/manifest/discover/inspect read-only) | `internal/sessadapter` (`CheckRequestBody`, `CheckSuccessBody`, `CheckFreshSink`) | landed sessadapter suite, green in this run |\n46|| Section 10.2 crash/idempotency discipline (fsync, atomic no-replace, quarantine) | `internal/localstore` | landed localstore fault suites, green in this run; delegation proven by `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` |\n47|| Closed-shape registry rows for these schemas | `internal/canonicaljson` (`rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape`, census-pinned) | intentionally not replaced; this package is the validating owner (see `doc.go`) |\n48|\n49|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n50|\n51|- Per-kind Canonical Event payload fact registries beyond the\n52|  Section 13.14.1 envelope in `checkPayload` (normalization sibling).\n53|- `maximal_safe` projection planning past\n54|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` (projection sibling).\n55|- Target-branch (G2) admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`.\n56|- Section 7.8 capture-plan/capture/normalize operation wiring\n57|  (stays `sessadapter`-owned).\n58|- `internal/traceability` registry bindings and digest re-pin\n59|  (Story FINAL leaf).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6f7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0d3-448d-7fa1-9a80-daada0956017"},"sequence":470,"recorded_at":1780531400000935,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0d44da174f8b61444b26fcd3c82","text":"Read text file `internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/clonebundle.\n3|\n4|Every gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\n5|weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n6|the named killer test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that\n7|the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n8|\n9|Each row runs M (mutate one production file in place), R (run the\n10|scoped Go killer through the production entry point), V (verdict from\n11|the Go exit code plus a FAIL kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test\n12|failure line, SURVIVED iff R passes, ERROR for anything else —\n13|unapplied patches, build breaks, timeouts). M failures and R\n14|infrastructure errors are ERROR, never kills or survivals. The file is\n15|restored from its backup after every row, pass or fail.\n16|\n17|Row C-doc-comment is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that\n18|must SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n19|hard-coding kills.\n20|\n21|Usage:\n22|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py\n23|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py N-raw-class\n24|\"\"\"\n25|\n26|import shutil\n27|import subprocess\n28|import sys\n29|import tempfile\n30|from dataclasses import dataclass\n31|from pathlib import Path\n32|\n33|REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n34|PACKAGE = \"internal/clonebundle\"\n35|\n36|\n37|@dataclass(frozen=True)\n38|class Mutant:\n39|    name: str\n40|    path: str\n41|    find: str\n42|    replace: str\n43|    count: int\n44|    run: str\n45|    expect: str\n46|    note: str\n47|\n48|\n49|MUTANTS = [\n50|    Mutant(\n51|        name=\"N-raw-class\",\n52|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/rawmanifest.go\",\n53|        find='\\t\"derived_cache_optional\",\\n\\t\"unknown\",\\n',\n54|        replace='\\t\"derived_cache_optional\",\\n\\t\"credential\",\\n\\t\"unknown\",\\n',\n55|        count=1,\n56|        run=\"TestRawManifestRefusals/build/credential_forbidden\",\n57|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n58|        note=\"Admits exactly credential into the raw subset; every other excluded class still refuses.\",\n59|    ),\n60|    Mutant(\n61|        name=\"N-raw-order\",\n62|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/rawmanifest.go\",\n63|        find=\"\\tif index > 0 && input.NativeItemKey <= previous {\\n\",\n64|        replace=\"\\tif index > 0 && input.NativeItemKey < previous {\\n\",\n65|        count=1,\n66|        run=\"TestRawManifestRefusals/build/duplicate_entries\",\n67|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n68|        note=\"Admits exactly duplicate keys; unsorted keys still refuse.\",\n69|    ),\n70|    Mutant(\n71|        name=\"N-exclusion-config\",\n72|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/rawmanifest.go\",\n73|        find=\"\\tif hosttrust.ExcludedConfigDirName(key) {\\n\",\n74|        replace=\"\\tif hosttrust.ExcludedConfigDirName(key) && false {\\n\",\n75|        count=1,\n76|        run=\"TestRawManifestExcludesTrustMaterial\",\n77|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n78|        note=\"Admits exactly the trust-adjacent config class; the replication matcher arm stays. Token preserved.\",\n79|    ),\n80|    Mutant(\n81|        name=\"N-sanitize-uuid\",\n82|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n83|        find=\"\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(key); err == nil {\\n\",\n84|        replace='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(key); err == nil && key != \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890c2\" {\\n',\n85|        count=1,\n86|        run=\"TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer\",\n87|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n88|        note=\"Admits exactly one UUIDv7 native key; every other UUIDv7 still refuses. Token preserved.\",\n89|    ),\n90|    Mutant(\n91|        name=\"N-always-excluded\",\n92|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/captureitem.go\",\n93|        find='\\tcase \"credential\", \"machine_auth\", \"runtime_state\", \"transient_lock\":\\n',\n94|        replace='\\tcase \"machine_auth\", \"runtime_state\", \"transient_lock\":\\n',\n95|        count=1,\n96|        run=\"TestCaptureItemRefusals/credential_included\",\n97|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n98|        note=\"Admits exactly included credential rows; the other three always-excluded classes still refuse.\",\n99|    ),\n100|    Mutant(\n101|        name=\"N-included-reason\",\n102|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/captureitem.go\",\n103|        find=\"\\t\\tif hasReason {\\n\",\n104|        replace='\\t\\tif hasReason && class == \"unknown\" {\\n',\n105|        count=1,\n106|        run=\"TestCaptureItemRefusals/included_with_reason\",\n107|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n108|        note=\"Admits exactly non-unknown included rows with a reason; the killer uses durable_payload.\",\n109|    ),\n110|    Mutant(\n111|        name=\"N-unknown-complete\",\n112|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/capturebuild.go\",\n113|        find=\"\\tif hasUnknownClass(items) {\\n\",\n114|        replace=\"\\tif hasUnknownClass(items) && len(items) > 4 {\\n\",\n115|        count=1,\n116|        run=\"TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete\",\n117|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n118|        note=\"Admits exactly small unknown-class manifests as complete; the 4-item killer derives true.\",\n119|    ),\n120|    Mutant(\n121|        name=\"N-excluded-exact\",\n122|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/capturebuild.go\",\n123|        find=\"\\tif len(derived) != len(excluded) {\\n\",\n124|        replace=\"\\tif len(derived) > len(excluded) {\\n\",\n125|        count=1,\n126|        run=\"TestExcludedClassesExactGate\",\n127|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n128|        note=\"Admits exactly superset excluded_classes; missing classes still refuse.\",\n129|    ),\n130|    Mutant(\n131|        name=\"N-proof-identity\",\n132|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/boundary.go\",\n133|        find=\"\\t\\tif proof.SnapshotIdentity != nil {\\n\",\n134|        replace='\\t\\tif proof.SnapshotIdentity != nil && proof.ProofKind != \"closed_store\" {\\n',\n135|        count=1,\n136|        run=\"TestBoundaryRefusals/decode_stable_proof/closed_store_with_identity\",\n137|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n138|        note=\"Admits exactly closed_store with an identity; provider_quiescence still refuses one.\",\n139|    ),\n140|    Mutant(\n141|        name=\"N-core-only\",\n142|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/boundary.go\",\n143|        find=\"\\t\\tif !input.Core {\\n\",\n144|        replace='\\t\\tif !input.Core && input.Generation != \"g\" {\\n',\n145|        count=1,\n146|        run=\"TestBoundaryRefusals/build_core-only_unstable\",\n147|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n148|        note=\"Admits exactly non-core unstable with generation g, the killer's generation.\",\n149|    ),\n150|    Mutant(\n151|        name=\"N-g2-generation\",\n152|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/boundary.go\",\n153|        find='''\\tif boundary.Kind == \"unstable_archive\" {\n154|\\t\\treturn invalid(\"capture boundary unstable_archive cannot enter a target branch\")\n155|\\t}\n156|''',\n157|        replace='''\\tif boundary.Kind == \"unstable_archive\" && boundary.SourceGeneration.String() != \"generation-9\" {\n158|\\t\\treturn invalid(\"capture boundary unstable_archive cannot enter a target branch\")\n159|\\t}\n160|\\tif boundary.Kind == \"unstable_archive\" {\n161|\\t\\treturn nil\n162|\\t}\n163|''',\n164|        count=1,\n165|        run=\"TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive\",\n166|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n167|        note=\"Admits exactly generation-9 unstable archives to the target branch; every other unstable still refuses.\",\n168|    ),\n169|    Mutant(\n170|        name=\"N-main-count\",\n171|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/session.go\",\n172|        find=\"\\tif mainCount != 1 {\\n\",\n173|        replace=\"\\tif mainCount < 1 {\\n\",\n174|        count=2,\n175|        run=\"TestCanonicalSessionRefusals/build_actors/two_mains\",\n176|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n177|        note=\"Admits exactly multi-main sessions at both build and decode sites; zero-main still refuses.\",\n178|    ),\n179|    Mutant(\n180|        name=\"N-synth-operation\",\n181|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/event.go\",\n182|        find=\"\\t\\tif !hasOperation {\\n\",\n183|        replace=\"\\t\\tif !hasOperation && hasNativeEvent {\\n\",\n184|        count=1,\n185|        run=\"TestCanonicalEventRefusals/evidence/synthesized_missing_operation\",\n186|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n187|        note=\"Admits exactly synthesized evidence with neither native event nor operation, the killer's shape.\",\n188|    ),\n189|    Mutant(\n190|        name=\"N-blob-size\",\n191|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/blobref.go\",\n192|        find=\"\\tif size != wantSize {\\n\",\n193|        replace=\"\\tif size != wantSize && size+1 != wantSize {\\n\",\n194|        count=1,\n195|        run=\"TestBlobAgreementRefusals\",\n196|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n197|        note=\"Admits exactly off-by-one size claims; every other disagreement still refuses.\",\n198|    ),\n199|    Mutant(\n200|        name=\"N-self-digest\",\n201|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/decode.go\",\n202|        find=\"\\tif calculated != claimed {\\n\",\n203|        replace='\\tif calculated != claimed && claimed.Hex() != \"ccdd35168ab474fa5764a526cfb83621351e23682c5075b2e18d56bddf96aa30\" {\\n',\n204|        count=1,\n205|        run=\"TestRawManifestRefusals/decode/self_digest_mismatch\",\n206|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n207|        note=\"Admits exactly the forged self digest sha256('forged'); every other mismatch still refuses.\",\n208|    ),\n209|    Mutant(\n210|        name=\"N-descriptor-claim\",\n211|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/blobref.go\",\n212|        find=\"\\tif calculated != claimed {\\n\",\n213|        replace='\\tif calculated != claimed && claimed.Hex() != \"edb3da2954b883ebc2099da18edeac4e12f8f5d67aa5bb2dd80ba472b23481f2\" {\\n',\n214|        count=2,\n215|        run=\"TestBlobAgreementRefusals\",\n216|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n217|        note=\"Admits exactly the forged descriptor claim at both agreement and install sites; every other mismatch still refuses.\",\n218|    ),\n219|    Mutant(\n220|        name=\"N-maximal-incomplete\",\n221|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/capturebuild.go\",\n222|        find=\"\\tif !manifest.RawComplete {\\n\",\n223|        replace=\"\\tif !manifest.RawComplete && hasUnknownClass(manifest.Items) {\\n\",\n224|        count=1,\n225|        run=\"TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation\",\n226|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n227|        note=\"Admits exactly incomplete known-class manifests to maximal_safe; unknown still blocks.\",\n228|    ),\n229|    Mutant(\n230|        name=\"C-doc-comment\",\n231|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/doc.go\",\n232|        find=\"// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, Sections\\n\",\n233|        replace=\"// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, Sections (control).\\n\",\n234|        count=1,\n235|        run=\"TestCaptureClassVocabularyIsPinned\",\n236|        expect=\"SURVIVED\",\n237|        note=\"Harmless control: a comment-only edit must survive.\",\n238|    ),\n239|]\n240|\n241|\n242|def run_mutant(mutant: Mutant) -> str:\n243|    target = REPO / mutant.path\n244|    original = target.read_text()\n245|    found = original.count(mutant.find)\n246|    if found != mutant.count:\n247|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: patch anchors {found}, want {mutant.count}\"\n248|    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as staging:\n249|        backup = Path(staging) / \"backup\"\n250|        shutil.copy2(target, backup)\n251|        try:\n252|            target.write_text(original.replace(mutant.find, mutant.replace))\n253|            run = subprocess.run(\n254|                [\"go\", \"test\", f\"./{PACKAGE}/\", \"-run\", mutant.run, \"-count=1\"],\n255|                cwd=REPO,\n256|                capture_output=True,\n257|                text=True,\n258|                timeout=300,\n259|            )\n260|        finally:\n261|            shutil.copy2(backup, target)\n262|    output = (run.stdout + run.stderr).strip()\n263|    if 'build failed' in output or '\\n# ' in output or output.startswith('# '):\n264|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: build broke under the patch\"\n265|    if run.returncode == 0:\n266|        verdict = \"SURVIVED\"\n267|    elif '--- FAIL' in output or 'FAIL:' in output:\n268|        verdict = \"KILLED\"\n269|    else:\n270|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: exit {run.returncode} with no kill line\"\n271|    mark = \"ok\" if verdict == mutant.expect else \"MISMATCH\"\n272|    return f\"{mark}: {mutant.name}: {verdict} (want {mutant.expect}) :: {mutant.note}\"\n273|\n274|\n275|def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n276|    selected = [m for m in MUTANTS if not argv or m.name in argv]\n277|    if argv and len(selected) != len(argv):\n278|        unknown = sorted(set(argv) - {m.name for m in selected})\n279|        print(f\"unknown mutants: {', '.join(unknown)}\")\n280|        return 2\n281|    failures = 0\n282|    for mutant in selected:\n283|        try:\n284|            line = run_mutant(mutant)\n285|        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n286|            line = f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: killer timed out\"\n287|        print(line, flush=True)\n288|        if not line.startswith(\"ok:\"):\n289|            failures += 1\n290|    return 1 if failures else 0\n291|\n292|\n293|if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n294|    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
