{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cbd9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0d3-448d-7fa1-9a80-daada0956017"},"sequence":1095,"recorded_at":1780531400002185,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0d9-47c5-7a83-a179-90f2f0a2f33a"},"task_id":"01a0b0d9-47c5-7a83-a179-90f2f0a2f33a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0d9-47c5-7a83-a179-90f2f0a2f33a","chunk":"Read text file `internal/environ/decode.go`.\n1|package environ\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"bytes\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"fmt\"\n7|\t\"io\"\n8|\t\"regexp\"\n9|\t\"strconv\"\n10|\t\"strings\"\n11|\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n12|\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n14|)\n15|\n16|// maxUint53 is the largest exactly representable JSON integer:\n17|// counts and limits are uint53 throughout the pinned\n18|// specification.\n19|const maxUint53 = uint64(1<<53 - 1)\n20|\n21|// Fault is one strict-decode failure: what was wrong and which\n22|// member it was found in, if any. It never carries foreign bytes.\n23|// The five details are the complete fault space: every body this\n24|// package refuses at the frame layer carries exactly one of them,\n25|// and the frame-agreement battery derives its denominator from\n26|// this list, so a sixth fault shape fails the census instead of\n27|// passing silently.\n28|type Fault struct {\n29|\tDetail string\n30|\tMember string\n31|}\n32|\n33|func (fault *Fault) Error() string {\n34|\tif fault.Member == \"\" {\n35|\t\treturn \"environment frame \" + fault.Detail\n36|\t}\n37|\treturn \"environment frame \" + fault.Detail + \" in member \" + fault.Member\n38|}\n39|\n40|// Frame fault details. Each is a constant so the agreement battery\n41|// derives the fault space from production source instead of\n42|// retyping it: a reworded fault fails its row rather than passing\n43|// against a stale copy.\n44|const (\n45|\tFaultNotUTF8       = \"not valid UTF-8\"\n46|\tFaultLoneSurrogate = \"lone surrogate escape\"\n47|\tFaultNotObject     = \"not a JSON object\"\n48|\tFaultDuplicate     = \"duplicate member\"\n49|\tFaultTrailing      = \"trailing data after the object\"\n50|)\n51|\n52|// DecodeStrictObject parses one complete JSON object with\n53|// duplicate member rejection. It is the only JSON entry point in\n54|// this package: every body crosses it before any member is read.\n55|// A non-UTF-8 frame, a lone surrogate escape, a non-object top\n56|// level, a duplicated member, or trailing data is a fault, never\n57|// a partial object the caller could mistake for a result.\n58|func DecodeStrictObject(data []byte) (map[string]json.RawMessage, *Fault) {\n59|\tif !utf8.Valid(data) {\n60|\t\treturn nil, &Fault{Detail: FaultNotUTF8}\n61|\t}\n62|\tif HasLoneSurrogateEscape(data) {\n63|\t\treturn nil, &Fault{Detail: FaultLoneSurrogate}\n64|\t}\n65|\tdecoder := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(data))\n66|\ttoken, err := decoder.Token()\n67|\tif err != nil {\n68|\t\treturn nil, &Fault{Detail: FaultNotObject}\n69|\t}\n70|\tdelim, ok := token.(json.Delim)\n71|\tif !ok || delim != '{' {\n72|\t\treturn nil, &Fault{Detail: FaultNotObject}\n73|\t}\n74|\tmembers := map[string]json.RawMessage{}\n75|\tfor decoder.More() {\n76|\t\tkeyToken, err := decoder.Token()\n77|\t\tif err != nil {\n78|\t\t\treturn nil, &Fault{Detail: FaultNotObject}\n79|\t\t}\n80|\t\tkey, ok := keyToken.(string)\n81|\t\tif !ok {\n82|\t\t\treturn nil, &Fault{Detail: FaultNotObject}\n83|\t\t}\n84|\t\tif _, duplicate := members[key]; duplicate {\n85|\t\t\treturn nil, &Fault{Detail: FaultDuplicate, Member: key}\n86|\t\t}\n87|\t\tvar raw json.RawMessage\n88|\t\tif err := decoder.Decode(&raw); err != nil {\n89|\t\t\treturn nil, &Fault{Detail: FaultNotObject, Member: key}\n90|\t\t}\n91|\t\tmembers[key] = raw\n92|\t}\n93|\tif token, err := decoder.Token(); err != nil {\n94|\t\treturn nil, &Fault{Detail: FaultNotObject}\n95|\t} else if delim, ok := token.(json.Delim); !ok || delim != '}' {\n96|\t\treturn nil, &Fault{Detail: FaultNotObject}\n97|\t}\n98|\tif _, err := decoder.Token(); err != io.EOF {\n99|\t\treturn nil, &Fault{Detail: FaultTrailing}\n100|\t}\n101|\treturn members, nil\n102|}\n103|\n104|// HasLoneSurrogateEscape reports whether the raw frame carries a\n105|// UTF-16 escape the JSON string grammar cannot pair. Go's\n106|// encoding/json would otherwise replace the lone escape with\n107|// U+FFFD silently, so wire bodies carrying lone surrogates would\n108|// be admitted with rewritten bytes.\n109|//\n110|// The walk is string-aware: only escapes inside JSON strings\n111|// count, and a backslash escape consumes both bytes, so the text\n112|// \"\\\\ud800\" (backslash-plus-text, JSON source `\"\\\\ud800\"`) is\n113|// not an escape and is admitted at the frame gate. A scanner\n114|// that matches every `\\u` byte pair regardless of string context\n115|// refuses that text, and worse, misreads it as a high surrogate\n116|// paired with a following real escape — admitting a real lone\n117|// escape the string walk refuses. The sessadapter and dirnode\n118|// facades once carried that raw scan and diverged in both\n119|// directions; they now delegate their frame verdict to\n120|// DecodeStrictObject, and the frame-agreement battery proves\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
