{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd05","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0d3-448d-7fa1-9a80-daada0956017"},"sequence":1245,"recorded_at":1780531400002485,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0dc-ea6c-75a1-ac08-ebad2ee0c08f"},"task_id":"01a0b0dc-ea6c-75a1-ac08-ebad2ee0c08f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0dc-ea6c-75a1-ac08-ebad2ee0c08f","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-24-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -40 LOGBOOK.md; echo =====; git diff HEAD -- LOGBOOK.md README.md | head -80; echo =====; git rev-parse HEAD; git ls-remote origin main 2>&1 | head -2\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK, README diff, and base currency\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-24z2b3 — clone bundle + canonical session/event types (first leaf)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/clonebundle` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture contracts over the landed owners — Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (Capture Items, Source Basis, Capture Boundary, core-derived `raw_complete`), Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (Source Evidence, raw refs, content blocks), NativeIdentity/WorkspaceBinding, immutable generations — plus Section 10.2 descriptor agreement and no-replace install via `localstore`. Every Build entry is byte-identical for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the closed shape. Row-21 exclusion allowlist (`hosttrust` matchers) enforced at raw-entry and capture-item construction with per-class negatives.\\n- OWNERSHIP: `canonicaljson` keeps its `rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows (that table's census pins every row); this package is the validating owner and reuses `Canonicalize`/`VerifyObjectIdentity` (blobs), `sessadapter.DecodeTuple`, `environ.CheckExtensions`, `scalar`, and `localstore.PutBlob`; blob identity uses `CalculateObjectIdentity` plus a local claim comparison and never the attesting `VerifyObjectIdentity` entry (provhost no-attestation bound). No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (82.2% statements), 17 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` proves the localstore delegation (double install agrees, tampered bytes refuse); durability itself is the landed localstore discipline (purity bound for this package: no second write path). README package section added with test commands and no capability claim.\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): per-kind event payload fact registries past the envelope; `maximal_safe` planning past the refusal gate; G2 admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`; Section 7.8 operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 18 of 18 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\\n- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); pre-existing 26 probes re-run green (neutral passed, client-cache documented SURVIVED). Per-plant logs/tables in the outcome tar.\\n- TRACEABILITY: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 suite tests; new `unevidenced` bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1 with honest gaps (executed lanes vs stated bounds); 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 stays unowned by design (no policy reader); digest re-pinned `e327bb08...`; report 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses; README figures + tracecheck pins updated.\\n- AC: 7 of 7 hostile rows + 13 of 13 executed AC-HOST-001 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed. NOTE: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` replay against `origin/main e4e3e88` fails on a LOGBOOK.md rebase conflict (missing replay resolution) — orchestrator-side integration issue, worktree untouched at `244a7dc`.\\n- 2026-09-17 rev3 on `fc67abd`: pin `d3eca906…`, report 132 cases / 65 bindings / 7 unowned / 49 of 535 clauses; harness denominator 24 prior + 9 new; refresh-candidate completed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2atgj4 — property-test the ownership reducer (final leaf)\\n\\n- SCOPE: executable proofs of the four story-pinned ownership invariants\\n  (union-order independence, loser preservation, clock non-authority,\\n  zero duplicate authorized owners) over `sessstate.Reduce`/`Compare`,\\n  `sessrepo.WinningLease`/`ListLeases`, and `fencing.Authorize*`\\n  (Sections 2.2, 5.3, 13.6-13.10, v0.6.0). Final leaf of\\n  STORY-260830-1oqfec; carries the story-close traceability,\\n  README, and registry re-pin items.\\n- DEFECT (RED-first): `resolveWinner` reported each losing union lease\\n  against the transient arrival-order winner, so a loser's\\n  divergent-history evidence — even its presence — depended on union\\n  order (witness: `{R@1, A@1}` on an empty chain reports the loss in\\n  one arrival order and drops it in the other). FIX: two-pass\\n  resolution — select the greatest tuple first, then report every\\n=====\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 43c6d21..93d48d4 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,6 +5,14 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-17\\n \\n+### TASK-260830-24z2b3 — clone bundle + canonical session/event types (first leaf)\\n+\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/clonebundle` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture contracts over the landed owners — Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (Capture Items, Source Basis, Capture Boundary, core-derived `raw_complete`), Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (Source Evidence, raw refs, content blocks), NativeIdentity/WorkspaceBinding, immutable generations — plus Section 10.2 descriptor agreement and no-replace install via `localstore`. Every Build entry is byte-identical for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the closed shape. Row-21 exclusion allowlist (`hosttrust` matchers) enforced at raw-entry and capture-item construction with per-class negatives.\\n+- OWNERSHIP: `canonicaljson` keeps its `rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows (that table's census pins every row); this package is the validating owner and reuses `Canonicalize`/`VerifyObjectIdentity` (blobs), `sessadapter.DecodeTuple`, `environ.CheckExtensions`, `scalar`, and `localstore.PutBlob`; blob identity uses `CalculateObjectIdentity` plus a local claim comparison and never the attesting `VerifyObjectIdentity` entry (provhost no-attestation bound). No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n+- EVIDENCE: package suite green (82.2% statements), 17 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` proves the localstore delegation (double install agrees, tampered bytes refuse); durability itself is the landed localstore discipline (purity bound for this package: no second write path). README package section added with test commands and no capability claim.\\n+- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): per-kind event payload fact registries past the envelope; `maximal_safe` planning past the refusal gate; G2 admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`; Section 7.8 operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+- AC: 18 of 18 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n+\\n ### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n - DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n - F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 1f8fc60..ca5639e 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -2383,6 +2383,33 @@ go test ./internal/matjournal -count=1 -cover\\n python3 internal/matjournal/mutant_harness.py\\n ```\\n \\n+## Clone Bundle and Canonical Session Types\\n+\\n+[`internal/clonebundle`](internal/clonebundle) validates and constructs\\n+the Section 13.14.1 clone capture contracts: Clone Raw Object Manifest\\n+1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 with its Capture Items, Capture\\n+Source Basis, and Capture Boundary, Canonical Session 1.0.0 with its\\n+Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 with Source Evidence and raw byte-range\\n+references, the NativeIdentity and WorkspaceBinding identities, and\\n+immutable source generations. Every Build entry produces byte-identical\\n+canonical bytes for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the\\n+closed shape, the class vocabularies, the included/excluded content\\n+rule, the core-derived `raw_complete` reconciliation, the stable-proof\\n+coupling, and the row-21 hosttrust exclusion allowlist. Blob Descriptor\\n+identity and byte-count agreement verify through `canonicaljson`, and\\n+blob bytes install only through the `localstore` no-replace discipline;\\n+the package performs no durable write itself. The clause map in\\n+[`internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`](internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md)\\n+maps every pinned clause to its production entry and test, with the\\n+sibling-owned bounds stated. It adds no `ax` command, no `doctor`\\n+result, and no runtime capability claim.\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1\\n+go test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1 -cover\\n+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py\\n+```\\n+\\n ## Crash/Restart Outcome Gate\\n \\n [`internal/crashgate`](internal/crashgate) executes the Section 13.13\\n=====\\n888ae3dff6a55c29bfaf311957748d405ed1ab06\\n888ae3dff6a55c29bfaf311957748d405ed1ab06\\trefs/heads/main\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 12220,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3055,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
