{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d815","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0d3-448d-7fa1-9a80-daada0956017"},"sequence":2661,"recorded_at":1780531400005317,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0eb08ec732cb521e0f3772054fb","text":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 61-63\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-| 13.14.1 reverse-DNS extensions, no normative reference | `encodeExtensions`, `checkExtensions` | contract round trips + `bad extensions` rows in every refusal table |\n-| 10.2 Blob Descriptor identity + byte-count agreement | `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` | `TestBlobAgreementRefusals`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` row |\n-| 10.2 no-replace install (fsync + verify + atomic) | `InstallRawBlob` via `localstore.PutBlob` | `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` |\n+| 13.14.1 reverse-DNS extensions, no normative reference | `encodeExtensions`, `checkExtensionsClosed` | contract round trips + `bad extensions` rows in every refusal table |\n+| 1.6 AX number model + nested duplicate refusal on extension values | `checkExtensionsClosed`, `checkExtensionValues`, `checkAXNumberLiteral` | `TestRawManifestRefusals/extension_values` (1.5, 2^53, 2^60, exponent, nested float/unsafe, nested duplicate incl. resealed) |\n+| 1.6 string measure in characters | `stringLength` via `environ` | `TestMultibyteStringMeasure` (300-char/600-byte admit, 512 admit, 513 refuse) |\n+| 13.14.1 one item per plan candidate at construction | `checkPlanItemMatch` | `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/build_plan_match` (extra, missing, renamed candidate) |\n+| 13.14.1 content block inline-XOR-descriptor | `checkContentBlocks` | `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/build_envelope` (neither, both) |\n+| 13.14.1 duplicate raw keys refused | `VerifyCaptureReconciliation`, `deriveRawComplete` | `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` (duplicate raw/plan keys, derive direct) |\n+| 13.14.1 source_identity_digest over sanitized bytes | `IdentityDigest` (re-decodes before hashing) | `TestIdentityDigestIsStable`, `TestIdentityDigestRefusals` (bad kind, bad extension key, unsanitized opaque/session) |\n+| 10.2 Blob Descriptor identity + byte-count agreement | `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` (with entry identity link) | `TestBlobAgreementRefusals`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `TestVerifyRawManifestDescriptorsRefusals` |\n+| 10.2 entry names the verified descriptor | `buildRawEntries`, `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` | build `descriptor id mismatch` row, `TestVerifyRawManifestDescriptorsRefusals` (fetch/absent/wrong/link) |\n+| 10.2 no-replace install (fsync + verify + atomic) | `InstallRawBlob` via `localstore.PutBlob` | `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent`, `TestInstallRawBlobRefusals` (forged claim, short/long bytes) |\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md","added":10,"removed":3},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d817","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0d3-448d-7fa1-9a80-daada0956017"},"sequence":2662,"recorded_at":1780531400005319,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f02750e1-95aa-4722-a114-f72ebe5c150a"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0eb205076eeafb5ff8c3c962c2a","text":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 86-90\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## Stated bounds (sibling scope)\n-\n-- Per-kind Canonical Event payload fact registries beyond the\n-  Section 13.14.1 envelope enforced in `checkPayload` (normalization\n-  sibling).\n+## Stated bounds (sibling scope)\n+\n+- Non-message Canonical Event payload member values past the\n+  envelope: `checkPayload` enforces strict objects and content-block\n+  rules, but per-kind fact values (including their numbers) are the\n+  normalization sibling's registry. Only `extensions` members carry\n+  the AX value model here.\n+- `-0` and leading-`+`/leading-zero integer literals in extension\n+  values admit, exactly as `canonicaljson.validateAXNumbers`\n+  admits them (`strconv.ParseInt` parity); the model refuses\n+  fractions, exponents, and magnitudes at or beyond 2^53.\n+- `BoundaryInput.Core` is caller-asserted; the real unstable-archive\n+  protection is `RefuseUnstableForTarget` at target admission.\n+- `InstallRawBlob`'s `blob_id`/`size` member-parse arms repeat the\n+  owner grammar after `CalculateObjectIdentity` already enforced\n+  it (`validateBlobDescriptor` requires digest `blob_id` and uint53\n+  `size`): defense in depth, unreachable on failure, pinned by the\n+  owner suite; the install negatives pin the claim comparison and\n+  the store size/digest enforcement end to end.\n+- Per-kind Canonical Event payload fact registries beyond the\n+  Section 13.14.1 envelope enforced in `checkPayload` (normalization\n+  sibling).\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md","added":22,"removed":5},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
